---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const effective = 'August 14, 2026';
const entity = 'Angel0x1';
const contact = 'privacy@angel0x1.com';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy — Angel0x1" description="How Angel0x1 handles your data: it stays on your device.">
  <main class="wrap legal">
    <a href="/" class="eyebrow back">← Back</a>
    <p class="soul legal-title">Privacy Policy</p>
    <p class="eyebrow faint">Effective {effective}</p>
    <p class="soft lead">
      This Privacy Policy explains how {entity} (“{entity},” “we,” “us”) handles your
      information when you use the {entity} app and this website. The short version:
      your journal lives on your device, we don’t run an account system, and we collect
      as little as possible. This policy describes that in full.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2 class="h3">1 · Information we collect</h2>
      <p class="soft">We keep collection to a minimum. The only information we may receive is:</p>
      <ul class="soft points">
        <li><strong>Reservation email</strong> — if you reserve an early-access spot, the email address you submit. We send a one-time code to it to confirm the address is yours.</li>
        <li><strong>A one-way hash of your IP address</strong> — when you reserve, we store a salted SHA-256 hash of your IP (never the IP itself) solely to prevent abuse and enforce fair per-network limits. It cannot be reversed back into your address.</li>
        <li><strong>Anonymous usage analytics</strong> — only if you turn analytics on. These are coarse, content-free events (for example, which screens are opened), tied to a random per-install identifier, never to your identity.</li>
        <li><strong>Purchase records</strong> — subscriptions are processed by Apple. We receive only Apple’s aggregate, anonymous sales reports; we never see or store your name, card, or billing details.</li>
        <li><strong>Basic diagnostics</strong> — if you contact us or if Apple shares crash reports you’ve opted into, we may receive standard technical information to fix problems.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="soft">We do not require an account, and we do not use advertising or third-party tracking.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="h3">2 · Information that never leaves your device</h2>
      <p class="soft">
        Your journal entries, the app’s AI reflections, moods, embeddings, voice
        transcriptions, any Health data, and the on-device model of your patterns are
        encrypted on your device (AES-256-GCM) and are <strong>never transmitted to us
        or anyone else</strong>. The encryption key is stored in your device’s secure
        keychain. We operate no server that can read this content, and the on-device AI
        runs locally — your writing is not sent to a model in the cloud.
      </p>
    </section>
    <!-- P_MARK -->

    <section>
      <h2 class="h3">3 · How we use information</h2>
      <ul class="soft points">
        <li>Your <strong>waitlist email</strong> is used only to contact you about the launch and early access — nothing else.</li>
        <li><strong>Anonymous analytics</strong> (if enabled) help us understand which features are useful and where the experience breaks, in aggregate.</li>
        <li><strong>Purchase records</strong> from Apple are used to keep your Pro access working across your devices.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="h3">4 · How information is shared</h2>
      <p class="soft">
        We do not sell, rent, or trade your information, and we do not share it for
        advertising. Limited processors act on our behalf: <strong>Apple</strong> handles
        payments and app delivery; our email and hosting providers store your waitlist
        email so we can reach you. We may disclose information if required by law, or to
        protect the rights, safety, and security of our users, the public, or {entity}.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="h3">5 · Data storage &amp; security</h2>
      <p class="soft">
        On-device content is encrypted with AES-256-GCM under a key held in your device
        keychain. Your waitlist email is stored with a reputable hosting provider using
        encryption in transit and at rest. No method of storage or transmission is 100%
        secure, but we design to collect little, so there is very little for anyone —
        including us — to lose.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="h3">6 · Your rights &amp; choices</h2>
      <ul class="soft points">
        <li><strong>Your journal:</strong> delete any entry, or use “erase everything” in the app for a cryptographic wipe. Uninstalling removes all local data.</li>
        <li><strong>Analytics:</strong> off by default — turn it on or off anytime in Settings.</li>
        <li><strong>Waitlist email:</strong> ask us to access or delete it anytime by replying to any message from us or emailing <a href={`mailto:${contact}`} class="ilink">{contact}</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Regional rights:</strong> depending on where you live (e.g. the EEA, UK, or California), you may have rights to access, correct, delete, or restrict the limited data we hold, and to lodge a complaint with your local authority. Contact us to exercise them; we don’t discriminate against you for doing so.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="h3">7 · Data retention</h2>
      <p class="soft">
        On-device content is kept until you delete it. A waitlist email is kept until the
        launch window closes or you ask us to remove it, whichever comes first. Anonymous
        analytics are retained only in aggregate and cannot be traced back to you.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="h3">8 · Children</h2>
      <p class="soft">{entity} is intended for people 17 and older and is not directed to children, and we do not knowingly collect information from them.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="h3">9 · International users</h2>
      <p class="soft">
        {entity} is available internationally. Because journal content stays on your
        device, it is not transferred across borders by us. Where limited data (a waitlist
        email) is processed, it may be handled by providers in other countries under
        appropriate safeguards.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="h3">10 · Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p class="soft">
        {entity} is an app in active, early-stage development — features evolve quickly,
        and occasional rough edges or issues are expected as it matures. If this policy
        changes materially, we’ll update the date above and, in the app, ask you to review
        it again. Continued use after an update means you accept the revised policy.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="h3">11 · Contact</h2>
      <p class="soft">
        Questions about privacy? Email <a href={`mailto:${contact}`} class="ilink">{contact}</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="eyebrow faint updated">Plain-language summary for your convenience — not a substitute for legal advice.</p>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal { max-width: 680px; padding-block: clamp(120px,16vh,180px) 120px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; }
  .legal-title { font-size: clamp(40px,7vw,72px); color: var(--ink); line-height: 1; }
  .legal .lead { margin: 10px 0 18px; font-size: 1.05em; }
  .legal section { padding-top: 22px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line-2); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; margin-top: 8px; }
  .legal .h3 { font-size: clamp(19px,2.4vw,24px); letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .legal .points { margin: 4px 0 0; padding-left: 20px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 9px; }
  .legal .points li { line-height: 1.55; }
  .legal .ilink { color: var(--red); }
  .legal .ilink:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .back { display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .updated { margin-top: 34px; }
</style>

  </main>
</Base>
